# Re: Automated Code Review — REQUEST_CHANGES (the original 2-blocker review)

Both blockers and the test-coverage gap from this review were fixed and pinned in the earlier rework rounds and remain green on the current head (now `78ae52e69`, the merge with main):

- stale-snapshot re-render over sanctioned mid-session writes → the `onUserConfigFileChanged` re-sync hook, now fired by ALL six direct USER-config writers (the two flows this review's successor thread added — ttsr/mcp — are wired in this round);
- `validateAgentSection` rejecting the emitter's `agent.misuseBreaker` → the mirror accepts `misuseBreaker` + `stuckTool` (this round additionally restructured into the `_agentKeyValidators` table so the new keys stop costing CRAP — see that thread);
- the inverse-invariant regression tests are in (reg group 16/16, config-service parity 77/77);
- both suggestions resolved (formatter-canonical wrap kept; the no-op-save pin is event-based).

See the replies to the CRAP-ratchet and hook-sweep threads for what this round added on top.

